WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.420
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.940
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.700
I'm Kurata Sana, I'm an actress in 1st year of middle school.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.360
My manager, Rei-kun.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.990
An American boy that looks completely like my former best friend, Brad.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.790
This person's a choreographer of Broadway that I've never seen before, Michelle Hamilton.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.790
My strongest ally in New York, Naozumi-kun.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.800
Help me!

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.300
You're in my way!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.170
Return to Japan at once!

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.470
Michelle.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.060
What is this supposed to mean?

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.980
Why did you call this kid?

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.690
You're doing too much on your own, I don't agree with this.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.190
And you're...

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:15.570
Help!

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.700
You shouldn't have come here.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.860
Go home!

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:23.990
You... just as you said... I was the one you were after...

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.870
What are you doing, Brad?

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.580
Are you alright, Naozumi?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.790
Yes.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.340
Excuse me, there should be a Naozumi Kamura registered here.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.720
Yes. Please excuse my rudeness,
but you are... ?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:47.560
I'm Naozumi's... mother.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.900
It Was A Suddenly
Appearing Mother

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.490
Brad, why did you do that?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.380
I'm sorry, Sana Kurata, Naozumi Kamura.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.470
I kept you waiting for a long time.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.600
On top of that you've come from a far place. I'm really sorry.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.470
Could it be?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.680
I'm Gary Hamilton.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.560
I'm really glad you came.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.270
Yes.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.400
Yes.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.480
It seems that a lot of things happened while I was away.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.190
It's your doing, isn't it, Brad?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.370
Say it clearly, Brad!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.080
Michelle! Wait.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.460
Naozumi, Sana, I'm sorry, but could you return home before us?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.420
Today's lesson is already over.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.420
But...

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.170
I won't let Brad do such a thing again.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.670
You don't have to worry about it.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.100
We'll talk about the details later.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.680
Excuse us, we'll return now.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.770
Brad!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.070
You owe me an explanation.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.070
Why did you attack Naozumi and Sana?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.200
Speak up! Brad!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.870
I wanted to keep Naozumi away from Sicil.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:33.000
You two know why. You're the ones who are embarrassed, aren't you?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.080
Brad, you...

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.170
That's why I was pushing them out in your place.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.970
It's none of your business!

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.090
Don't get close to these two kids anymore,

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:52.980
or else you and Ramsy won't be welcome in my house anymore.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.190
You got that?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.980
I got it.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.280
Welcome back.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.690
Thank you.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.780
Thank you very much.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.070
There's a guest for Kamura-sama.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.990
A guest?

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:09.870
Who can it be?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.660
I don't know...

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.670
I didn't ask her name, but she was a beautiful lady.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.960
Is that so?

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.880
Hoho, a beautiful one.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.170
Sana-chan!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:24.260
- Perhaps she's one of your fans.
- There aren't any in New York!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.970
This boy doesn't accept ornaments at all...

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.140
It's not 'Ornaments', it's 'Attentions'.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.290
Hello.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.970
I'll return to my room.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.380
Babbit too...

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.270
Naozumi...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.230
Yes...

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.700
After all this time, I'm not asking you to forgive me.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:36.160
But there hasn't been a single day where I haven't thought about...

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.870
The day I got separated from you...

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:45.460
You were wearing white baby clothes, smiling while looking at me.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.880
Even now I clearly remember it.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.890
At that time, I was really poor.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.470
I had no money to even buy you milk.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.770
If it could have been solved by not eating myself, I could have managed.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.400
But to have to hear your hungry cries was painful.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.860
I did it for your sake!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:16.660
I had planned to get you back. Right after leaving your father, I went to America...

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:21.790
But right after I arrived, I became ill...

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.380
My only reason to live was to meet you once again.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.880
As a mother, I wanted to meet you.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.760
It's true. I truly wanted to...

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.480
Um...

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.360
I've got an appointment right now...
I have to go.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.990
I see...

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:54.870
It's true...

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.870
I suddenly came to see you...

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.370
Telling you I'm your mother after all this time-

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.670
Excuse me.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.960
Naozumi!

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.460
This is my address and telephone number.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.090
We'll meet again, won't we?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.390
...won't we?

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.980
Naozumi...

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.750
What's that?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.580
S-stop it! Release me!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.090
This woman...

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.680
Could it be that she's Naozumi-kun's...

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.390
Cologne has been put on my bottom...

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.260
Ah, Naozumi-kun's back.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.680
Well, doesn't matter...

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.900
Hi, it's Kurata Sana!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.570
Hello, hello?

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.860
Ho, it's Rei-kun!
What's the matter?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.570
Huh? You found one?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:21.080
Moving into the apartment

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.570
Anyways, read the user's manual carefully.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.040
Green floral, it's nice.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.210
Hey, you guys are Japanese, aren't you?

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.580
Yes, yes, that's right.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.590
I come from Japan too!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:33.460
I saw the movie 'Taxi Driver' and I couldn't stay still.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.180
So I came to New York, it was two years ago I think...

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.590
Tchapin and Katchan chabin fu fu bushuuu...

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.930
Don't get lost! Take care!

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:46.270
If you wander into strange places in this town and get lost, you'll have troubles.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.560
People say it's safe to ride taxis...

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:54.570
Since I'm doing this job, I should be used to the smell of make-up.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:58.700
Somehow... I couldn't stand it...

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.780
Here, here...

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.160
What's that, Sana-chan?
It smells good.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.790
Green Floral.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:09.130
It calms you down. Perhaps you prefer the trumpet...

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:13.090
...but it's useful when you can't play the trumpet...

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:16.090
Thank you.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:23.180
By the way, where are we going? What was it... Ah! I remember, I remember!

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:27.180
I wonder where it's located, the apartment Sagami-san has found...

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.400
Ah! We're here!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.070
Hehehe... I won't show it to you...

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:36.280
Black Babbit, you're mean!

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:40.070
While we were saying that, Sana-chan got in!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.160
It seems quite old, don't you think?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.370
Yes... So, room 3025... there it is!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.300
Rei-kun, Rei-kun! We've arrived!

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.840
Yes!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.010
Welcome!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.260
We've been waiting for you.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.390
Tsumo tsumomomomo...

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.890
In the garden there are birds.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.190
The shop closes at 12 o'clock.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.770
I'd like to go on a trip to Kononkania.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.360
Sorry, it seems we've made a mistake.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.070
Ah, Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun, that was fast.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:18.690
Rei-kun!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:19.990
Sagami-san!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:22.360
Then...

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.280
So, come in.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.660
Come in!

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.500
Who is this person?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:42.010
{parte b}

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:45.100
Babbit's Counting Song

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.570
What do you think about it? It's not a bad room, right?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.700
Yeah, it's good. Don't you think so, Naozumi-kun?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.570
Yeah, it's good...

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.570
So, who's that person?

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.160
Ah, he is-

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.290
"He?"

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.160
Everyone, let's have some tea!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.170
He was a man...

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.290
You didn't see it, Sana-chan?

00:12:56.210 --> 00:13:00.460
Rest

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.460
He's a half like me!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.380
This is Bernadette, living next door.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.090
Call me Bernie.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.470
I'm Sana, nice to meet you.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.970
I'm Naozumi, very pleased to meet you.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.600
I'm Babbit.

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:15.190
When I was in the city, I was embarrassed about not finding a room.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:18.110
He said the room next to his was free, it helped me a lot.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.690
I fell for Rei at first sight.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:26.570
The curtains and such were brought here by Bernadette, the furniture as well.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:31.290
You're really happy, Rei, living with such cute children.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.500
Can you do something about this 'tsun tsun'?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:38.960
I don't know your situation, but even if you've got no mama, you've got a papa, so it's okay.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.170
Even if it's painful, you must endure it.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.880
Eh? Papa?

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:46.130
Could it be that 'Papa'?
No, that's not it!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.970
You're not a father with his children? Then...

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.470
Shall I explain?

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:54.270
During the explanations

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.180
It's a strange story.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:59.560
So, it's like that!
Then, you're still single?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.570
It's true, but please stop the 'Tsun Tsun'.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.480
It's perfect!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.860
Stop it, Bernie...

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.070
What are we going to eat for dinner?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.370
Yes, what shall we do?

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.370
Pan and meat?

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.120
If you're talking about the dinner, I've already done it.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.590
It will be done soon, so expect something good.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.880
I don't want it anymore.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:28.380
But you've hardly eaten any.
You don't feel well?

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.180
I hate fish.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.390
Is that so?

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.760
Today I hate it.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:38.770
If it were hamburgers, I'd eat it.
Everyone's eating it, I want to try it too.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.980
If it's hamburger, you'll eat it?

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.270
I'd eat it!

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.570
Please go and buy some immediately.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.190
Understood.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.320
Bring it to my room.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.660
I'll be going.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.000
Don't think I'm spoiling her.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.160
I'm not thinking that.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.960
It's better than having her eat nothing.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:13.760
What's she thinking?
I understand her less and less...

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.190
Where are you going, Brad?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.990
I'm not going anywhere.
I'll be right back.

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.870
You're not planning anything secretly, are you?

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:39.870
If you keep on spoiling the Master and Mistress's mood, next time you'll really be unwanted here.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.670
I won't do anything that would sadden mama!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.090
Don't worry, I'll be right back.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.550
Brad...

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.390
What's up?

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:56.600
We found out where the Japanese people are going to move.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.390
A dirty apartment.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.230
What? That's all?

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:02.390
Huh? Didn't you want to know?

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.900
We tried really hard to find it!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.690
No, it's good work.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.610
Listen...

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:29.670
Sicil-chan's laughter sounds like an angel...

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.920
Ahh, it's nice...

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.760
If you have something to say, say it!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.560
Thanks for the food!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.060
Delicious!

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:51.070
I'm relieved! It's a special sauce that mama taught me, but I'm glad you like it.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.860
Naozumi? Perhaps you didn't like it?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:59.370
No, I'm sorry. I don't feel like eating.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:04.080
It's incredibly delicious, Naozumi-kun! Try a bit of it, and you'll see.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.460
I'm sorry, it smells good...

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.960
But I can't touch it...

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.300
Can't you at least drink the soup?

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.380
I'm sorry.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:17.470
Um... I...

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.770
I'm sorry. I'll go rest now.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.060
Because the omelette was tasty...

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.570
I was delighted about that...

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:34.860
I'm stupid, don't you think? I didn't think about Naozumi-kun's feelings.

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.570
That's not good...

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.780
Something... happened...?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:45.580
I'm sorry. I don't understand enough of the situation to explain it to you...

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.960
Oh, I have to go to the shop.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:50.790
Shop?

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.380
Odoru Burger Shop.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.760
Sana, I'll make an omelette sandwich so that it'll be easy to eat.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.590
Please take care of the rest.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.680
Right.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.690
Naozumi-kun, may I?

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:17.700
Sana-chan...? Come in.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.990
It's an omelette sandwich.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.160
Bernie made them.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.370
I'll put them here, ok?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.460
Thank you, but...

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.300
You're hungry, Naozumi-kun?

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.470
Eh? No...

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.260
You're hungry, right?

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:43.600
What's happened, Sana-chan?

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.190
You can eat it tomorrow when you want, ok?

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.060
If you don't want to eat it, leave it.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.190
I'll eat it tomorrow morning.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.980
The sandwich will be dry.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.910
I'll eat it anyway, so don't force yourself.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.200
Bye!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:05.870
Sana-chan!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.500
Thank you.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.790
It's nothing!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.090
Naozumi-kun...

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.670
When you want to talk, I'll listen.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.470
Ok...

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.360
Lesson Lesson!

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.480
You've got a big heart!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:35.190
Perhaps.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.780
Ok, 5 minute break!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.490
So suddenly?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.990
We're always on break, aren't we?

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:46.080
So, shall we go?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.490
Eh? You're going to skip the lesson?

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.160
Let's go dancing.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.880
Set ok!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:57.670
I'm ready!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.170
Let's dance!

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.180
Ahh... I've got a headache!

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:44.970
I'd like to be dancing more...

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:49.390
But it would be bad to sneak out of too many lessons.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.480
Sana-chan, that woman yesterday was my mother.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:53.770
Heh?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:57.770
But it's not my problem.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.780
I don't need a mother.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:02.860
I don't want to know the circumstances of my abandonment.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.160
Get out!

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.580
Wait a minute!

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:14.870
If you're here I can't bring Naozumi! You're embarrassing me! Get out!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:18.590
You can say that, but I can't find an apartment so fast, and...

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.800
Why don't you stay with your friends?

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.380
It's only a matter of 1 or 2 months.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.380
Is it really only for 1 or 2 months?

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:26.590
Yes.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:31.100
